hildren to get Western education  and they do that consciously and some of  them are able to give them a bit of  their old traditional identity that  doesn't interfere with our Western  curriculum some of them rejected  altogether my mother rejected it all  together deep in her heart she told my  father  if you send my your daughters to school  and you keep them in school they're  going to talk back to you they're going  to be rebellious they're going to do  things that you don't want them to  and she was completely right education  Western education made me rebellious  made me talkback made me run away made  me lead my own life so it's very  important for us when we talk about  education to identify which type of  education and which type of education do  we encourage and the education system  that I've come to encourage is that  Western form of Education it's  interesting the roles played by your  parents because most cases but not  always you will have mothers who want to  see their daughters educated fully and  to be able to advance themselves and  have vocational opportunities and make  choices for themselves and at times  we've witnessed in certain societies  where usually the father hasn't always  been that forthcoming but you are  mentioning that in your case your father  was encouraging an educational path a  Western medical Western educational path  but your mother was concerned about what  that would do she was concerned and her  concern was if you educate your children  Western Sal they'll become like  Westerners and move away from our  traditions and from our from our  religion and she was right in that now  they're not all Muslim women are like my  mother not all Muslim families are like  my family  some of them somehow find a  reconciliation between giving their  children a Western education and at the  same time keeping them within the clan  loyalties and within the Islamic  religion the loyalties that is a small  group what I have noticed especially